    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 120 ft, Devil's Sight (sees through magical darkness)",
    "tactics": "Shadow Hounds hunt. They use Death Sense to identify the most vulnerable target, Shadow Meld to approach unseen, and converge on weakened enemies. They ignore the summoner's allies unless those allies attack them, instinctively prioritizing wounded prey. This is their nature and not something negotiable.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Bite [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 2), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 8 damage (4 + 4 Str) + 2 Negative damage (Half DR)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 8 damage, DR halved (round up) + 2 Negative damage; target makes Fortitude [Easy] save or gains Weakened condition until end of their next turn.</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 3:</strong> 8 damage, DR halved (round up) + 2 Negative damage; Weakened condition, no save.</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Shadow Meld: In dim light or darkness, the Shadow Hound has Fortune on Stealth checks and ### Attacks against it add 1 to both dice. Pack Hunt: When an ally is within 5 feet of the target, the Shadow Hound subtracts 1 from both attack dice. Death Sense: The Shadow Hound automatically detects creatures below half HP within 60 feet.</p>",
